147
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:19,120
I own property on this street, Mahogany Road.

148
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:21,120
This issue has been a problem for many years.

149
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,120
It's been ongoing.

150
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:27,120
This is relatively minor, what you see here in these pictures.

151
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,120
Generally, there's three or four piles.

152
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:38,120
Much of it came from two property managers who managed properties for out-of-state investors.

153
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:45,120
I believe 90-20 may still be, and 90-14 were both owned by out-of-state investors, New

154
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,120
York Investment Group.

155
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,120
They didn't care.

156
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:53,120
Huntsville Property Management doesn't care, doesn't want to talk about garbage.

157
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:57,120
Those piles can sit out there for months, months and months.

158
00:08:57,120 --> 00:09:02,120
There can be all kinds of things out there, dirty toilets, rubbish in the street.

159
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:05,120
At least that's not even on the street.

160
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:12,120
There'll be bins full of water, mosquitoes flying around.

161
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,120
It goes on.

162
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:18,120
There are dogs eating the garbage out of torn bags.

163
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:26,120
Now, the issue, it's better now than it has been in years, I think in part to Jenny Robinson here.

164
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:32,120
But the issue is not just the piles of trash or the bulk items.

165
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:34,120
There is no bulk item pickup.

166
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:37,120
This is a commercial street.

167
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:40,120
This street is entirely commercial residential.

168
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:43,120
So there's commercial pickup only.

169
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:46,120
There is no bulk item pickup that I'm aware of.

170
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:49,120
I know by the city there is none.

171
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:54,120
This is not the only street with this condition.

172
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:57,120
There's a cotton row.

173
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:00,120
There's another one.

174
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:12,120
All dominated by a couple of, you'll see a pattern of the same property managers with this kind of situation going.

175
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:24,120
Now, the magnet for all of this is that the cans are allowed to sit out on the street 24-7, 365 days a year.

176
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:26,120
They're never removed.

177
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:32,120
You can see some buildings will have dumpster like you can see in the photo there.

178
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,120
And that's the way to go.

179
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:40,120
But they rely on individual cans for these tenants to come out to the street, fill them up, overflow.

180
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,120
They're out there day and night.

181
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,120
It is a blight in itself.

182
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:46,120
I've been to the city many times.

183
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:48,120
I've been in community development for years.

184
00:10:48,120 --> 00:11:03,120
I've had best luck with the county of Madison County Department of Public Health, who comes out every time I call the next day and they'll respond and give them 30 days.

185
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:09,120
Now, these things are in violation of multiple city codes.

186
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:13,120
I've gone through a thousand pages of your city code here.

187
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:24,120
And everything ranging from must provide a place to store garbage on the property.

188
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:32,120
Many things, maintenance of premises, litter, deposit of waste in the streets or gutters, demolition and construction waste.

189
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:46,120
Section 2233, Section 2236, 37, 42, 71, 72, 77, 79, 84 and 85 are all addressed the situation.

190
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:51,120
And they have never been looked at by the city as a whole.

191
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:55,120
Like I say, the magnet is the trash cans.

192
00:11:55,120 --> 00:12:00,120
When a tenant has a large bulk item they need to get rid of, where do they take it to?

193
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:02,120
They take it to the garbage can, of course, like everybody else.

194
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:06,120
Where is that? That's out in the street where it sits and then it collects.

195
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:07,120
And then more people see it.

196
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:10,120
They bring more stuff out and it just gets bigger and bigger and bigger.

197
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,120
I'd like to see this.

198
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:17,120
Now, community development tells me they can do nothing once the junk hits the street.

199
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:24,120
It becomes a sanitation department problem, but the sanitation department refuses to do anything about it.

200
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:34,120
I don't know how that happens or how the sanitation department makes this call and can't be brought to bear to do something.

201
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,120
But you've got to go after the garbage cans.

202
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:40,120
That pile is already gone as of today.

203
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:46,120
But the cans will remain and this will just be an ongoing issue.

204
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:51,120
Like I say, I've been watching this for going on seven years now personally.

205
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,120
It affects my tenants.

206
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,120
It affects me.

207
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:57,120
It affects the quality of tenant that I can attract to my units.

208
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:59,120
And it costing me money.

209
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:03,120
I'm embroiled in a lawsuit over it right now with another property manager.

210
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,120
It's gotten that bad.

211
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:09,120
The city needs to do something about it and needs to crack down on those cans.

212
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,120
And that's all I'm going to say.

213
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,120
Thank you.

214
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:13,120
Thank you, sir.

